# Pennyroyal native starter configuration.
# Copy to ~/.config/pennyroyal/pennyroyal.env (or any path you pass as
# --config / PENNYROYAL_CONFIG) and edit, or run ./configure-penny to generate
# it interactively. The recipes in configs/pennyroyal stay authoritative for
# inference flags; this file only says where things live and which options the
# recipe should see. Plain KEY=value lines, read as data — never shell-sourced
# or eval'd — so spaces, '$', and quotes survive.
#
# Precedence: --config PATH wins over PENNYROYAL_CONFIG, which wins over this
# default location. A key saved here wins over an inherited environment
# variable. A key that is not saved keeps the value it inherited, or the
# recipe's own default: unset means "the recipe decides". Nothing is rewritten
# behind your back and no hidden state is kept elsewhere.

# Which recipe to run: next (default — Flash-Next with native NEXTN MTP and
# the FR-Spec token map), next-plain (the same without FR-Spec), next-dflash2
# (the optional DFlash2 profile: the separate Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2
# draft, FR-Spec, routed widths), or 27b. Saved profile choices are always
# preserved; someone who picked next-dflash2 keeps it.
PENNYROYAL_PROFILE=next

# Your checkout and the environment that holds sglang. The recipes use
# $REPO_ROOT/.venv/bin/sglang, so VENV_PATH is usually all you need.
REPO_ROOT=/path/to/pennyroyal
VENV_PATH=/path/to/pennyroyal/.venv

# Downloaded checkpoints. Both DFlash2 profiles need a target and a draft; the
# native-MTP profiles use TARGET_MODEL only. Absolute paths, or paths
# relative to REPO_ROOT. The draft below is for the optional DFlash2 profiles;
# for 27b, use your 27B FP8 target and /models/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 instead.
TARGET_MODEL=/models/RadixArk-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4
DRAFT_MODEL=/models/incoai-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2

# Disk cache tier: on (the qualified default) keeps the persistent NIXL FILE
# cache under NIXL_STORAGE_BASE. off drops only the disk tier — the GPU radix
# cache, the host-RAM HiCache tier, the model and the speculation settings all
# stay as they are, nothing is deleted, and NIXL_STORAGE_BASE is then neither
# required nor created. The budget below is a cap on that cache: 0 means no
# cap, which is NOT the same as NIXL=off.
NIXL=on

# Writable roots. The recipes create the cache subdirectories under CACHE_BASE;
# ./run-penny --check tells you the exact mkdir command when one is missing.
CACHE_BASE=~/.cache/pennyroyal
NIXL_STORAGE_BASE=~/.local/share/pennyroyal/nixl

# GPU for the model, as an index from nvidia-smi or a UUID. Exported as
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, so the recipes keep their own single-GPU default.
GPU=0

# Soft byte budget for the NIXL FILE cache's configured dirs, in GiB. 0 means
# no cap: the persistent NIXL cache stays enabled and keeps growing; it does
# not disable the cache.
SGLANG_HICACHE_NIXL_MAX_CACHE_GB=0

# --- Advanced (optional): delete the leading '#' to change a value. ----------
# These are existing recipe variables; the defaults shown are what the recipes
# already use. Enabling any of them is a deliberate choice, not tuning you get
# for free, and none of them is chosen automatically for your hardware.

# PLE placement: ram (default) or nvme with a prepared snapshot.
#PENNY_PLE_BACKEND=ram
#PENNY_PLE_NVME_MODEL=/models/flash-next-ple

# Native-MTP width policy for the next and next-plain profiles: tiered (the
# qualified default: block 8 at one running request, block 4 at every batch of
# two or more), adaptive (the v3.0.2 policy: block 4 or 8 at one request under
# the existing 40/80 batch hold and backoff, block 4 at two or more) or
# fixed-w4 (block 4 at every concurrency). One value picks both the bundled
# policy file and the launch width that can carry it (steps 7 with 8 draft
# tokens for the two wider policies, steps 3 with 4 draft tokens for fixed-w4),
# so nothing has to be kept in step by hand; the selected policy's hash is part
# of the NIXL namespace. Unset keeps tiered, and unset is also where the shell
# form applies: with nothing saved here,
#   PENNY_MTP_POLICY=fixed-w4 ./run-penny
# launches that policy; saving it makes this file the answer, as it does for
# every other setting. The DFlash2 profiles route their own widths and read
# nothing from this.
#PENNY_MTP_POLICY=tiered

# Online FP8 is selected automatically on eligible Flash-Next SM120 launches.
# Only set the saved private override to pin the original precision (false)
# or force the conversion (true); see FP8.md.
#SGLANG_SM120_ONLINE_MXFP8=false

# Media preprocessing device: cpu (default) or cuda:N for a second GPU.
#SGLANG_MM_PREPROCESS_DEVICE=cpu
#SGLANG_FORWARD_UNKNOWN_TOOLS=true

# Request/state capacity and the optional shared KV cap. Unset = recipe default
# (4/24 requests and slots on the NEXTN profiles, 6/36 on the Flash-Next
# DFlash2 profile, whose draft verifies a whole block per request; 27b pins
# 4/24 in its own recipe) and a KV pool sized from the memory the engine
# profiles on every profile; an exported MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS is the operator's own
# cap, honored by all four recipes, and must be positive and page-64-aligned.
# The optional six-request profile is a coherent documented choice (6/36,
# requested 1048576; online FP8 engages automatically on an eligible SM120
# host), not a hardware-fit guarantee.
#MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=4
#MAX_MAMBA_CACHE_SIZE=24
#MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS=

# The Flash-Next DFlash2 verify width is not a knob: it is routed per batch
# size by the bundled configs/pennyroyal/adaptive-dflash2.json (block 6 for a
# single request, block 4 for two or more), and the launch carries the widest
# routed width. The 27b draft keeps its own fixed block 8.

# Host-RAM HiCache tier, in decimal GB (1 GB = 1e9 bytes, not GiB). Unset or
# blank keeps the recipe's qualified default: 32 for the Next profiles, 96 for
# 27b. A value must be a positive integer (>= 1). This RAM cache is separate
# from the PLE embedding table, which has its own placement above, and from
# the compiled-cache folders under CACHE_BASE.
#PENNY_HICACHE_SIZE_GB=32

# WSL2 host-memory workaround: true allocates the HiCache host pool as pinned
# host memory, the workaround for HiCache transfers under WSL2. Unset or false
# keeps the default host-register allocator used on native Linux.
#SGLANG_HICACHE_TORCH_PINNED_ALLOC=false

# First-start compile jobs (recipes default to 4) and a NIXL install prefix
# outside the system linker path.
#PENNY_BUILD_JOBS=4
#NIXL_PREFIX=/opt/nvidia/nvda_nixl

# Tensor-parallel ranks: unset keeps the profile's qualified TP1 (TP2 also
# needs a second GPU and a dedicated preprocessor device stays cpu).
#TP_SIZE=
